    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00008",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     7,
     1
    ],
    "text": "[B26]Note:[/B26]",
    "placeholders": {
     "B26": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00009",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     7,
     3
    ],
    "text": "This requirement is an extension to the ISO&nbsp;C standard, which allows [I27]getenv[/I27]() to copy the data to an internal\nbuffer.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I27": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00010",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     9,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I28]secure_getenv[/I28]() function shall be equivalent to [I29]getenv[/I29](), except that it shall return a null pointer if the\ncalling process does not meet all of the following security criteria:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I28": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I29": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00011",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     9,
     3,
     1,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The effective user ID and real user ID of the calling process were equal during program startup.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00012",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     9,
     3,
     3,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The effective group ID and real group ID of the calling process were equal during program startup.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00013",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     9,
     3,
     5,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Additional implementation-defined security criteria.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00014",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     23
    ],
    "text": "[A30][/A30]RETURN VALUE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A30": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_210_04\" id=\"tag_17_210_04\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00015",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     25,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Upon successful completion, [I31]getenv[/I31]() shall return a pointer to a string containing the value for the specified\n[I32]name[/I32]. If the specified [I33]name[/I33] cannot be found in the environment of the calling process, a null pointer shall be\nreturned.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I31": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I32": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I33": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00016",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     25,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[S34][[A35]CX[/A35]][/S34] [IMG36]\nUpon successful completion, [I37]secure_getenv[/I37]() shall return a pointer to a string containing the value for the specified\n[I38]name[/I38]. If the specified [I39]name[/I39] cannot be found in the environment of the calling process, or the calling process does\nnot meet the security criteria listed in DESCRIPTION, a null pointer shall be returned. [IMG40]",
    "placeholders": {
     "S34": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A35": {
