   {
    "id": "h4_00024",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     43
    ],
    "text": "[A46][/A46]RATIONALE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A46": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_210_08\" id=\"tag_17_210_08\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00025",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I47]clearenv[/I47]() function was considered but rejected. The [A48][I49]putenv[/I49]()[/A48] function\nhas now been included for alignment with the Single UNIX Specification.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I47": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A48": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/putenv.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I49": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00026",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     3
    ],
    "text": "Some earlier versions of this standard did not require [I50]getenv[/I50]() to be thread-safe because it was allowed to return a\nvalue pointing to an internal buffer. However, this behavior allowed by the ISO&nbsp;C standard is no longer allowed by POSIX.1.\nPOSIX.1 requires the environment data to be available through [I51]environ[/I51][], so there is no reason why [I52]getenv[/I52]() can't\nreturn a pointer to the actual data instead of a copy. Therefore [I53]getenv[/I53]() is now required to be thread-safe (except when\nanother thread modifies the environment).",
    "placeholders": {
     "I50": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I51": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I52": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I53": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00027",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     5
    ],
    "text": "Conforming applications are required not to directly modify the pointers to which [I54]environ[/I54] points, but to use only the\n[A55][I56]setenv[/I56]()[/A55], [A57][I58]unsetenv[/I58]()[/A57], and [A59][I60]putenv[/I60]()[/A59] functions, or assignment to [I61]environ[/I61] itself, to manipulate the process\nenvironment. This constraint allows the implementation to properly manage the memory it allocates. This enables the implementation\nto free any space it has allocated to strings (and perhaps the pointers to them) stored in [I62]environ[/I62] when [A63][I64]unsetenv[/I64]()[/A63] is called. A C runtime start-up procedure (that which invokes [I65]main[/I65]() and\nperhaps initializes [I66]environ[/I66]) can also initialize a flag indicating that none of the environment has yet been copied to\nallocated storage, or that the separate table has not yet been initialized. If the application switches to a complete new\nenvironment by assigning a new value to [I67]environ[/I67], this can be detected by [I68]getenv[/I68](), [A69][I70]setenv[/I70]()[/A69], [A71][I72]unsetenv[/I72]()[/A71], or [A73][I74]putenv[/I74]()[/A73] and the implementation can at that point reinitialize based on the new environment.\n(This may include copying the environment strings into a new array and assigning [I75]environ[/I75] to point to it.)",
    "placeholders": {
     "I54": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A55": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/setenv.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I56": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A57": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/unsetenv.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I58": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A59": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/putenv.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I60": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I61": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I62": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A63": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/unsetenv.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I64": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I65": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I66": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I67": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I68": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A69": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/setenv.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I70": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A71": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/unsetenv.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I72": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A73": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/putenv.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I74": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I75": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00028",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     7
    ],
    "text": "In fact, for higher performance of [I76]getenv[/I76](), implementations that do not provide [A77][I78]putenv[/I78]()[/A77] could also maintain a separate copy of the environment in a data structure that\ncould be searched much more quickly (such as an indexed hash table, or a binary tree), and update both it and the linear list at\n[I79]environ[/I79] when [A80][I81]setenv[/I81]()[/A80] or [A82][I83]unsetenv[/I83]()[/A82] is invoked. On implementations that do provide [A84][I85]putenv[/I85]()[/A84], such a copy might still be worthwhile but would need to allow for the fact that\napplications can directly modify the content of environment strings added with [A86][I87]putenv[/I87]()[/A86]. For example, if an environment string found by searching the copy is one that was\nadded using [A88][I89]putenv[/I89]()[/A88], the implementation would need to check that the string in\n[I90]environ[/I90] still has the same name (and value, if the copy includes values), and whenever searching the copy produces no match\nthe implementation would then need to search each environment string in [I91]environ[/I91] that was added using [A92][I93]putenv[/I93]()[/A92] in case any of them have changed their names and now match. Thus, each use of\n[A94][I95]putenv[/I95]()[/A94] to add to the environment would reduce the speed advantage of having the\ncopy.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I76": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A77": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/putenv.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I78": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I79": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A80": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/setenv.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I81": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A82": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/unsetenv.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I83": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A84": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/putenv.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I85": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
