   {
    "id": "p_00029",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     9
    ],
    "text": "Performance of [I96]getenv[/I96]() can be important for applications which have large numbers of environment variables. Typically,\napplications like this use the environment as a resource database of user-configurable parameters. The fact that these variables\nare in the user's shell environment usually means that any other program that uses environment variables (such as [A97][I98]ls[/I98][/A97], which attempts to use [I99]COLUMNS ),[/I99] or really almost any utility ([I100]LANG ,[/I100] [I101]LC_ALL\n,[/I101] and so on) is similarly slowed down by the linear search through the variables.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I96": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A97": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../utilities/ls.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I98": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I99": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I100": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I101": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00030",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     11
    ],
    "text": "An implementation that maintains separate data structures, or even one that manages the memory it consumes, is not currently\nrequired as it was thought it would reduce consensus among implementors who do not want to change their historical\nimplementations.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
